• Root cause is two-layered.

  | Layer | test35 | test49 |
  |---|---|---|
  | Immediate code-edge result | Code edge artifacts were admitted into event flow, assessed, and later re-entered/found/replayed. | Worker wrote files,
  but postflight rejected the report before hook/event admission. |
  | Failure semantics | Failure became runtime truth: proof/closure/continuation events. | Failure stayed in the operator archive as postflight_failed;
  no retry/continuation event was appended. |
  | Re-entry mechanism | Runtime could select/re-enter the same edge from event truth. | CLI returns next_action: repair_worker_output; operator/human
  must restart manually. |
  | Gap payload | Prior artifact state and proof pressure were visible to later traversals. | Blocking reason is a flat string list; not a machine-
  consumable repair dossier. |

  Immediate defect: path contract mismatch.

  The code worker wrote files under the right tenant root, but reported relativePath as workspace-relative:

  build_tenants/scala_spark/cdme-compiler/src/main/scala/...

  The TS postflight expects relativePath to be relative to the tenant root:

  cdme-compiler/src/main/scala/...

  That check is here: odd_sdlc/build_tenants/typescript/code/src/operator/handoff.ts:405. It computes relative(tenantRoot, absolutePath) and rejects
  mismatch at odd_sdlc/build_tenants/typescript/code/src/operator/handoff.ts:416.

  Deeper root cause: TS does not promote postflight failure into ABG continuation truth.

  The installed operator handles failed postflight here: odd_sdlc/build_tenants/typescript/code/src/operator/installed_operator.ts:435. It returns:

  status: postflight_failed
  nextLawfulAction: repair_worker_output
  emittedRuntimeEventKinds: []

  So ABG replay never receives “code edge failed with these repair obligations.” gaps still shows current edge derive_code_surface, but the reason lives
  in an archive, not in the graph’s continuation algebra.

  That is why test35 continued and test49 did not.

  Test35’s derive_code_surface sequence had event truth around dispatch, artifact observation, assessment, proof, closure, edge convergence, and later
  replay/found records. Test49’s failed code edge has a postflight archive but no appended failure/continuation event.

  So the fix is not “make Codex try again.” The fix is:

  postflight failure -> admitted gap dossier -> ABG retry/continuation event -> same-edge re-entry with prior artifacts + repair reasons

  And separately tighten the manifest wording/API so materializedFiles.relativePath is unambiguously tenant-root-relative.

